power: pmic: rk8xx: mark fuel gauge uninitialized on plug-in shutdown

With ROCKCHIP_RK8XX_DISABLE_BOOT_ON_POWERON (set in
anbernic-rgxx3-rk3566_defconfig), plugging a charger into a powered-off
device boots U-Boot just far enough for rk8xx_off_for_plugin() to see
ON_SOURCE = plug-in and shut straight back down, leaving the PMIC
charging the battery with no OS ever running.

That brief power cycle restarts the RK817 gas gauge with a coulomb
counter (Q_INIT/Q_PRES) that only the kernel ever seeds - and the
kernel never ran. On the next real boot, rk817_charger's restore path
trusts Q_PRES whenever the gauge's off-counter reads under 30 minutes
(its own comment: "we shouldn't ever encounter an OFF_CNT more than 0
on a reboot anyway" - an assumption this kernel-less boot violates),
computing capacity from an unseeded counter: the battery reads 0%
until the next full charge, and the only recovery is re-initializing
the gauge by hand or disconnecting the battery.

Set GG_STS bit 4 (BAT_CON, the "battery uninitialized" flag the
kernel driver checks at probe) before shutting down, so the next boot
takes the same first-boot path used on a fresh battery insert and
re-estimates the charge from an OCV voltage lookup instead. The
learned full-charge capacity is re-guessed from design capacity on
that path, which is the documented mainline behavior for an
uninitialized gauge and strictly better than a false empty reading.

Only the plug-in shutdown path is touched - normal boots and normal
poweroffs keep the gauge state exactly as before.

---
--- a/include/power/rk8xx_pmic.h
+++ b/include/power/rk8xx_pmic.h
@@ -212,6 +212,9 @@
 #define RK817_POWER_EN_SAVE0	0x99
 #define RK817_POWER_EN_SAVE1	0xa4
 
+#define RK817_GAS_GAUGE_GG_STS	0x57
+#define RK817_BAT_CON		BIT(4)
+
 #define RK806_RST_FUN_MSK	GENMASK(7, 6)
 
 #define RK806_POWER_EN(x)			(0x00 + (x))
--- a/drivers/power/pmic/rk8xx.c
+++ b/drivers/power/pmic/rk8xx.c
@@ -79,6 +79,17 @@ void rk8xx_off_for_plugin(struct udevice *dev)
 	case RK817_ID:
 		if (pmic_reg_read(dev, RK817_ON_SOURCE) & RK8XX_ON_PLUG_IN) {
 			printf("Power Off due to plug-in event\n");
+			/* This shutdown leaves the PMIC charging with no OS
+			 * ever having run to seed the gas gauge's coulomb
+			 * counter, which the OS would otherwise trust on the
+			 * next boot and read as an empty battery. Flag the
+			 * gauge uninitialized so the next boot re-estimates
+			 * the charge from the battery voltage instead.
+			 * RK809 shares this code path but has no gas gauge.
+			 */
+			if (priv->variant == RK817_ID)
+				pmic_clrsetbits(dev, RK817_GAS_GAUGE_GG_STS,
+						0, RK817_BAT_CON);
 			pmic_clrsetbits(dev, RK817_REG_SYS_CFG3, 0,
 					BIT(0));
 		}
